<title>FRANCE: UAP first-half net attributable rises.</title>
<headline>UAP first-half net attributable rises.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half 1996.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of French francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net attributable			     860  vs	     806</p>
<p>Of which:</p>
<p>     Insurance				   2,029  vs	   1,774</p>
<p>    Banking activity			    245  vs		61</p>
<p>	of which:	Banque Worms   loss   26  vs     loss   63</p>
<p>			   BNP			255  vs	     125</p>
<p>    Other				   loss  145  vs     loss   32</p>
<p>    Result of operating companies	 2,129  vs	    1,803</p>
<p>    Holding companies		   loss  776  vs     loss   422</p>
<p>    Amortization of goodwill		  493  vs		575</p>
<p>Note: Analysts were expecting a profit in the region of 750 to 800 million francs but said disposals could alter those figures.  </p>
<p>UAP's 1995 result was a loss of 2.065 billion francs, which included an exceptional charge of 4.5 billion francs written into second-half results.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
